1
00:00:00,145 --> 00:00:02,279
This is the Wall of ScrappyT.

2
00:00:03,012 --> 00:00:04,120
Its signature Cent,

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:08,000
number 7139, was struck in 1967,

4
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:11,519
carries a full desert patina, and is a Ghost Cent.

5
00:00:11,599 --> 00:00:13,519
Ghost means a full or near-full

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:16,000
patina sets Lincoln apart from the field.

7
00:00:16,079 --> 00:00:17,600
Of the thirty-three Ghost Cents,

8
00:00:17,679 --> 00:00:20,399
only thirteen carry a full desert patina.

9
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:22,800
The Wall holds 41 Cents in two

10
00:00:22,879 --> 00:00:25,839
wallets, from 1956 to 1982,

11
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,440
which puts it in the Quarter Club,

12
00:00:27,519 --> 00:00:29,760
for twenty-five to forty-nine Cents.

13
00:00:29,907 --> 00:00:31,280
One of them is a wheat penny,

14
00:00:31,359 --> 00:00:33,280
minted 1958 or earlier,

15
00:00:33,399 --> 00:00:35,200
with two ears of wheat on the back.

16
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:38,640
It is from 1956, the earliest year on the Wall.

17
00:00:38,713 --> 00:00:41,119
It holds three Cents from 1971,

18
00:00:41,159 --> 00:00:42,880
for the 1971 Club.

19
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:45,119
Two of its Cents carry a full patina:

20
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,200
the full desert and a full red.

21
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:48,640
Two are Iridescent,

22
00:00:48,719 --> 00:00:50,159
a copper surface overlaid

23
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,240
with gold, violet and blue.

24
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,000
And two are Ghost Cents.

25
00:00:54,073 --> 00:00:56,159
The Wall completes six Sets.

26
00:00:56,232 --> 00:00:57,359
A Spectrum Set:

27
00:00:57,399 --> 00:00:58,799
a significant verdigris,

28
00:00:58,826 --> 00:01:00,320
a significant obsidian,

29
00:01:00,359 --> 00:01:02,320
a full red, a full desert,

30
00:01:02,359 --> 00:01:04,480
a notable gold and an orange.

31
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:07,040
Notable means clearly visible but local,

32
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:09,599
significant a major presence on the face,

33
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:12,560
and full means the patina dominates the coin.

34
00:01:12,706 --> 00:01:15,840
As of October 2026, ScrappyT is one of only

35
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,640
fifteen collectors to hold a Spectrum Set.

36
00:01:18,712 --> 00:01:19,840
A Chronicle Set:

37
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:24,719
a Cent from 1971, from 1979 and from 1982.

38
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:26,079
A Full Mint Set:

39
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,599
an S mint, a D mint and a Cent with no mint mark.

40
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:31,120
A Contamination Set,

41
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,719
four of the twelve contamination

42
00:01:32,879 --> 00:01:34,480
types: special oddities,

43
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,920
obscure adhesive, speckles and alien secretion.

44
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,599
And a 1970s Set

45
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,200
and a 1980s Set:

46
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:44,480
every mint year from 1970 to 1982.

47
00:01:44,552 --> 00:01:46,560
The Wall carries Diamond Hands:

48
00:01:46,599 --> 00:01:48,159
it has held its position for at least

49
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:50,319
a year, with little to no selling.

50
00:01:50,612 --> 00:01:52,560
And it is a Mint Keeper: ScrappyT

51
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,000
minted four of its Cents

52
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:56,400
and still holds them, never sold.

53
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,920
Find all of the Collector Walls

